    "headline": "Gas tank $242 a year vs electric tank $564",
    "explain": "With U.S. average prices, a gas tank (standard vent) costs $321 a year less to run than an electric tank. The cheapest type to run is a heat pump (hybrid), 240 V at $138 a year ($12 a month). Use: 55 gallons a day heated by 62.0 °F.",
    "formula": "Rise = 120 °F − 58.0 °F incoming = 62.0 °F\nHeat per year = 55 gal × 365 × 8.34 lb × 62.0 °F = 10,380,381 BTU\nGas: therms = heat ÷ 100,000 ÷ UEF; × $1.481/therm\nElectric: kWh = heat ÷ 3,412 ÷ UEF; × $0.1723/kWh\nGas tank (standard vent) (UEF 0.64): 164 therms → $242/yr\nElectric tank (UEF 0.93): 3,271 kWh → $564/yr\nHeat pump (hybrid), 240 V (UEF 3.80): 801 kWh → $138/yr\nGas tankless (UEF 0.95): 109 therms → $162/yr\nElectric tankless (UEF 0.92): 3,307 kWh → $570/yr",
